IMPORT prelude

-- International Child Abduction Act 2010 (Singapore) -- when the Hague Convention applies to a child (s 4, Arts 3, 4), when a
-- Singapore court must order a wrongfully removed child returned and when it may refuse (Arts 12, 13, 17, 18, 20), the Central
-- Authority route (ss 6, 7, 21, Art 27), the court route (ss 8, 11, 13, 14), legal aid and advice (ss 17, 18), and who pays
-- (s 23, Art 26).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 1/4/2022", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ICAA2010.txt. The latest amendment annotated is
-- s 8(4), "[Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]". The Schedule reproduces only some Articles of the Convention; the rest are shown as
-- "... ... ..." (Arts 2, 6, 11, 16, 23, 25 and 33 onward are not in the deposited Schedule).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: a parent who takes a child across a border without the other parent's
-- consent, or a parent left behind, meets this Act. SCOPED to the provisions such a parent meets. Not encoded: the Gazette list
-- of Contracting States and their in-force dates (s 4(1), not in the deposit), territorial declarations (s 4(3)), the Minister as
-- Central Authority (s 5), intervention (s 9), interim orders beyond their effect on s 13 (s 10), welfare advice (s 12), the
-- means test and procedure imported from the Legal Aid and Advice Act 1995 (s 19), proof of documents (s 22), regulations
-- (ss 20, 24), and the Convention's Central Authority duties (Arts 7, 9, 10, 21) except as they shape ss 6 and 7.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `International Child Abduction Act 2010 -- return of abducted children`

§§ `s 4 and Articles 3, 4 -- does the Convention apply, and was the removal wrongful`

-- Art 4: "The Convention shall apply to any child who was habitually resident in a Contracting State immediately before any
-- breach of custody or access rights. The Convention shall cease to apply when the child attains the age of 16 years."
-- s 4(2): unless the Minister's order provides otherwise, the Convention applies between Singapore and a Contracting State "only
-- in relation to (a) wrongful removals or retentions of children; or (b) breaches of access rights to children, occurring on or
-- after" the date the order specifies.
-- Art 3: removal or retention is wrongful where "(a) it is in breach of rights of custody ... under the law of the State in which
-- the child was habitually resident immediately before the removal or retention; and (b) at the time of removal or retention
-- those rights were actually exercised, either jointly or alone, or would have been so exercised but for the removal or
-- retention." Art 5(a): rights of custody include "the right to determine the child's place of residence".
DECLARE `Return case` HAS
    `age of the child` IS A NUMBER
    `habitually resident in a Contracting State before the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
    `breach on or after the Convention came into force between the two States` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in breach of custody rights under the law of habitual residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `those rights were exercised or would have been but for the removal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months from removal to the start of proceedings` IS A NUMBER
    `the child is now settled in its new environment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the left-behind parent consented or later acquiesced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `grave risk of harm or an intolerable situation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child objects and is of an age and maturity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
    `return offends fundamental principles of human rights` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a custody order in the abductor's favour exists in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `c` IS A `Return case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Convention applies to the child` IF
        `c`'s `age of the child` LESS THAN 16
    AND `c`'s `habitually resident in a Contracting State before the breach`
    AND `c`'s `breach on or after the Convention came into force between the two States`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Return case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the removal or retention is wrongful` IF
        `c`'s `in breach of custody rights under the law of habitual residence`
    AND `c`'s `those rights were exercised or would have been but for the removal`

§§ `Articles 12, 13, 17, 18 and 20 -- must the Court order return`

-- Art 12: where "a period of less than one year has elapsed from the date of the wrongful removal or retention" at the
-- commencement of proceedings, "the authority concerned shall order the return of the child forthwith". After one year it
-- "shall also order the return of the child, unless it is demonstrated that the child is now settled in its new environment".
-- Art 13: the authority "is not bound to order the return" if the opposer establishes (a) the custodian "was not actually
-- exercising the custody rights ... or had consented to or subsequently acquiesced"; or (b) "a grave risk" of "physical or
-- psychological harm or otherwise ... an intolerable situation"; and "may also refuse" if "the child objects to being returned
-- and has attained an age and degree of maturity at which it is appropriate to take account of its views".
-- Art 20: return "may be refused if this would not be permitted by the fundamental principles of the requested State relating to
-- the protection of human rights and fundamental freedoms".
-- Art 17: "The sole fact that a decision relating to custody has been given in or is entitled to recognition in the requested
-- State shall not be a ground for refusing to return a child".
-- Art 18: the Chapter does "not limit the power ... to order the return of the child at any time" -- so a refusal ground makes
-- return DISCRETIONARY, never forbidden.
-- Time is counted here in whole months: under 12 months is "less than one year". (Art 13(a)'s "not actually exercising" overlaps
-- Art 3(b) and is carried by the wrongfulness test, not repeated here.)
GIVEN `c` IS A `Return case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `less than one year had elapsed` IF
    `c`'s `months from removal to the start of proceedings` LESS THAN 12

GIVEN `c` IS A `Return case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ground to refuse return is made out` IF
        ((NOT `less than one year had elapsed` `c`) AND `c`'s `the child is now settled in its new environment`)
    OR  `c`'s `the left-behind parent consented or later acquiesced`
    OR  `c`'s `grave risk of harm or an intolerable situation`
    OR  `c`'s `the child objects and is of an age and maturity to be heard`
    OR  `c`'s `return offends fundamental principles of human rights`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Return case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court must order return` IF
        `the Convention applies to the child` `c`
    AND `the removal or retention is wrongful` `c`
    AND (NOT `a ground to refuse return is made out` `c`)

GIVEN `c` IS A `Return case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court may refuse return` IF
        `the Convention applies to the child` `c`
    AND `the removal or retention is wrongful` `c`
    AND `a ground to refuse return is made out` `c`

§§ `ss 6, 7, 21 and Article 27 -- the Central Authority route`

-- s 6(1): a claim that a child "has been wrongfully removed to or retained in Singapore" in breach of custody rights under the law
-- of a Contracting State -> the Central Authority's "assistance in facilitating the voluntary return of the child or an amicable
-- resolution". s 6(2): a claim that a child has been wrongfully removed to or retained in a Contracting State in breach of rights
-- under the law of Singapore -> "to have the person's claim sent to the Central Authority of the Contracting State".
-- s 7(1): access rights under a Contracting State's law to a child in Singapore -> assistance "in facilitating an amicable
-- resolution". s 7(2): access rights under Singapore law to a child in a Contracting State -> claim sent abroad.
-- The Act gives no Central Authority route for a child taken to a State that is not a Contracting State.
DECLARE Situation IS ONE OF
    `custody breached and child brought into Singapore`
    `custody breached and child taken from Singapore to a Contracting State`
    `access breached and child in Singapore`
    `access breached and child in a Contracting State`
    `child taken to a State that is not a Contracting State`

DECLARE Help IS ONE OF
    `help with voluntary return or amicable resolution`
    `help with amicable resolution of access`
    `claim sent to the foreign Central Authority`
    `no Central Authority route under the Act`

GIVEN `the situation` IS A Situation
GIVETH A Help
`what the Central Authority of Singapore offers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the situation`
    WHEN `custody breached and child brought into Singapore` THEN `help with voluntary return or amicable resolution`
    WHEN `custody breached and child taken from Singapore to a Contracting State` THEN `claim sent to the foreign Central Authority`
    WHEN `access breached and child in Singapore` THEN `help with amicable resolution of access`
    WHEN `access breached and child in a Contracting State` THEN `claim sent to the foreign Central Authority`
    OTHERWISE `no Central Authority route under the Act`

-- s 6(4): the Central Authority "may accept" a custody application from "(a) the person to whom the rights of custody ... are
-- attributed" or "(b) any other person appearing ... to have sufficient interest in the matter"; (6) "person" includes an
-- institution or other body. ss 6(5), 7(4): it "may refuse to accept" an application "not submitted in accordance with this
-- section or section 21 or for any of the reasons specified in Article 27". s 21: a document "in a language other than English"
-- must be "accompanied by an English translation". Art 27: not bound to accept "When it is manifest that the requirements of this
-- Convention are not fulfilled or that the application is otherwise not well founded".
-- (Acceptance is a discretion: this rule says when refusal is NOT open, i.e. when the application cannot be turned away on the
-- statutory grounds.)
GIVEN `holds the custody rights` IS A BOOLEAN, `has sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the specified form` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in English or with an English translation` IS A BOOLEAN, `manifestly ill-founded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the custody application is safe from refusal` IF
        (`holds the custody rights` OR `has sufficient interest`)
    AND `in the specified form`
    AND `in English or with an English translation`
    AND (NOT `manifestly ill-founded`)

§§ `ss 8, 11, 13 and 14 -- the court route`

-- s 8(2): an application for return "may be made by (a) the person to whom the rights of custody ... are attributed ... or (b) any
-- person appearing to the Court to have sufficient interest in the matter". (3): the applicant "must notify the Central Authority
-- of Singapore ... as soon as practicable". Art 29: the Convention does not preclude applying directly to the court.
GIVEN `holds the custody rights` IS A BOOLEAN, `has sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply to the Court for return` IF
    `holds the custody rights` OR `has sufficient interest`

-- s 11(1): "where an application under section 8 for the return of a child is pending or has been dismissed by the Court, the
-- Court may issue an injunction restraining any person from taking the child out of Singapore". s 8(4): if the Court determines
-- the child should be returned it may "give permission for the child to be taken out of Singapore".
DECLARE `Application status` IS ONE OF
    `no application made`
    `application pending`
    `application dismissed`
    `return ordered`

GIVEN `the status` IS A `Application status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an injunction under s 11 is available` IF
    CONSIDER `the status`
    WHEN `application pending` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `application dismissed` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 13(1): once a s 8 application is made, "no decision may be made by any court in respect of the custody of, care and control of
-- or access to the child in any proceedings until the Court has determined the application". (3): this does not limit interim
-- orders under s 10. (4): "court" includes "the Syariah Court and the Appeal Board" under the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966.
GIVEN `a return application is undetermined` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is an interim order under s 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a custody, care and control or access decision may be made` IF
    (NOT `a return application is undetermined`) OR `it is an interim order under s 10`

-- s 14(1): on an application "for the purpose of Article 15 of the Convention by any person appearing to the Court to have
-- sufficient interest", the Court may declare that "the removal of a child from Singapore, or the retention of the child outside
-- Singapore, was wrongful".
GIVEN `the child was removed from or kept out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `has sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `wrongful under Article 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court may declare the removal wrongful` IF
    `the child was removed from or kept out of Singapore` AND `has sufficient interest` AND `wrongful under Article 3`

§§ `ss 17, 18 -- legal aid and legal advice`

-- s 17: the Director "may grant legal aid in connection with any proceedings under section 8 or 14 to any person (a) who is a
-- citizen of, or habitually resident in, Singapore or a Contracting State; and (b) who is or will be (i) a party to the proceedings
-- under section 8; or (ii) the applicant in the proceedings under section 14."
-- s 18: oral advice on Singapore law in connection with the Convention, and help preparing a legal aid application, for "any
-- person who is a citizen of, or habitually resident in, Singapore or a Contracting State".
-- s 19 imports the Legal Aid and Advice Act 1995 (including, presumably, its means test -- an inference; not encoded).
DECLARE Connection IS ONE OF
    `Singapore citizen`
    `habitually resident in Singapore`
    `citizen of a Contracting State`
    `habitually resident in a Contracting State`
    `no link to Singapore or a Contracting State`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `applicant for return under s 8`
    `parent resisting return under s 8`
    `applicant for a declaration under s 14`
    `respondent to a declaration under s 14`

GIVEN `the connection` IS A Connection
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a qualifying connection` IF
    CONSIDER `the connection`
    WHEN `no link to Singapore or a Contracting State` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the connection` IS A Connection, `the role` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be granted legal aid under the Act` IF
        `has a qualifying connection` `the connection`
    AND CONSIDER `the role`
        WHEN `respondent to a declaration under s 14` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the connection` IS A Connection
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may receive legal advice under the Act` IF
    `has a qualifying connection` `the connection`

§§ `s 23 and Article 26 -- who pays`

-- s 23: "No costs mentioned in Article 26 of the Convention are to be borne by the Government, the Central Authority of Singapore
-- or any other public authority in Singapore except insofar as they fall to be so borne by virtue of the grant of legal aid or
-- advice under Part 4."
GIVEN `covered by legal aid or advice under Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government bears the applicant's Article 26 costs` IF
    `covered by legal aid or advice under Part 4`

-- Art 26 (last paragraph): "Upon ordering the return of a child or issuing an order concerning rights of access ... the judicial or
-- administrative authorities may, where appropriate, direct the person who removed or retained the child ... to pay necessary
-- expenses incurred by or on behalf of the applicant, including travel expenses, any costs incurred or payments made for locating
-- the child, the costs of legal representation of the applicant, and those of returning the child."
DECLARE Expense IS ONE OF
    `the applicant's travel expenses`
    `the cost of locating the child`
    `the applicant's legal representation`
    `the cost of returning the child`
    `the abductor's own legal costs`

GIVEN `the expense` IS A Expense, `a return or access order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the abductor may be directed to pay` IF
        `a return or access order was made`
    AND CONSIDER `the expense`
        WHEN `the abductor's own legal costs` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
